    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_message">OpenDoJa For Android (unofficial port)\nVersion: %1$s\nPort by: Wandering Hunter\n\nThis is an unofficial Android port of \"OpenDoJa\". Wandering Hunter ported it using the free versions of OpenCode and Xiaomi Mimo V2.6. This version exists only because Wandering Hunter wanted to play these games on an Android handheld, and tried porting them based on the OpenDoJa 0.25 source code.\n\nFor now, the compatibility of OpenDoJa For Android cannot be compared with the Windows version of OpenDoJa. This is a temporary stopgap; I have almost nothing to do with emulator development, so you are advised to wait for the official Android version of OpenDoJa.\n\nThanks:\nThe Android port referenced the JAR2DEX implementation from the open-source JL-MOD code. Thanks to the developers of JL-MOD and J2ME Loader.\nThanks to Magstic for ideas, issues and answers about some DoJa APIs during development.\nThanks to the people in the Keitai World Discord for dumping and maintaining the handsets; without you this project would not exist.\nFinally, thanks to the OpenDoJa developers. Without the OpenDoJa project I could never have attempted this Android port.\n\nThis port is open source under GPL V3.\nGithub: https://github.com/liulang-delieren/OpenDoJa-for-Android-Unofficial-Port-</string>
